      title: 'A mission starts on two agreements and its day-one checklist',
      item1:
        'A mission’s page now shows, before it starts, the client agreement, the consultant agreement, the signed contract or purchase order, the assigned consultant, the start date, the daily rate and day-one access — each with its own state, and a verdict: ready, ready with reservations, blocked or incomplete.',
      item2:
        'Moving a mission to “ready to start” (or from onboarding straight to running, board included) is now refused while a blocking prerequisite is missing — and the refusal names each one. Creating a mission is never blocked: it simply shows “agreements to confirm”.',
      item3:
        'Each agreement or prerequisite is confirmed by hand with its proof (email, purchase order, call), dated and signed; an agreement older than 60 days has to be revalidated. Withdrawing one archives it, it is never deleted.',
